Article 6 (Contents and Methods of Assessment of Impacts of Climate Change on Fisheries and Fishing Villages, etc.)
(1) Investigation and assessment of the impacts of climate change on fisheries and fishing villages and the resulting vulnerability under Article 35-2 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "climate impact assessments, etc.") shall include the following:
1. Abnormal changes in weather and climate affecting fisheries and fishing villages;
2. Changes in suitable areas and productivity for fisheries and aquaculture;
3. Changes in occurrence and damage from disasters, accidents, aquatic animal diseases, and infectious diseases of aquatic organisms;
4. Changes in diversity of fisheries resources;
5. Changes in fishing villages, including population and income of residents;
6. Other matters deemed by the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries necessary to be included in climate impact assessments, etc. for sustainable development of fisheries and fishing villages.
(2) Climate impact assessments, etc. and fact-finding surveys under Article 35-2 (2) of the Act shall be conducted according to a plan including timing, scope, methods, etc.
(3) Climate impact assessments, etc. and fact-finding surveys shall be conducted by direct surveys such as observation, experiments, or questionnaires, and indirect surveys using relevant data.
(4) Before publicly announcing the results of climate impact assessments, etc. pursuant to Article 35-2 (1) of the Act, the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall undergo review by the Fisheries and Fishing Villages Climate Impact Assessment Advisory Committee under Article 7.
(5) Public announcement of the results under paragraph (4) shall be made by posting them on the Internet website of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries.
